formula:
  title: "Cryptographic Hash Function Principle"
  expression: "H = Hash(M)  |  Where H is fixed-size digest, M is variable-length message"
  explanation: "A cryptographic hash function maps arbitrary-length binary data to a fixed-length hexadecimal digest. Ideal hash functions are deterministic, fast to compute, non-reversible (pre-image resistance), collision-resistant (no two messages yield the same digest), and exhibit an avalanche effect where a 1-bit input change alters over 50% of the output bits."
